From 8fad3aff6730587c46ad2a4f04ad18c81e79ce50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:15:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban consent: stops follow compression lineage;
 fence worker kanban_comment and summary edits

Follow-up to PR #1783 review 5886701099 (points 5-7):
5. session_stops walks the parent_session_id lineage (bounded, cycle-safe),
   so a stop recorded before context compression binds cards created after
   the session id rotates; a later same-target approval still supersedes it.
6. A worker's kanban_comment tool (HERMES_KANBAN_TASK set) refuses a target
   its card's creation stops or its run session's stops cover
   (rejection consent_stop), closing the direct same-board comment path.
7. kanban edit of a done run's summary refuses a new gated delivery claim
   unless the prior summary made it or the admitted receipt proves it.
Remaining known limits are documented in hermes_cli/kanban_consent.py.
